# 高频词汇 List10
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List10核心词汇

acquire /əˈkwaɪə(r)/ v. 获得；学到 She acquired a new skill through practice. 她通过实践获得了一项新技能。
administer /ədˈmɪnɪstə(r)/ v. 管理；执行 The committee administers the scholarship fund. 委员会管理奖学金基金。
adverse /ˈædvɜːs/ adj. 不利的 Adverse weather conditions affected the harvest. 不利的天气条件影响了收成。
advocate /ˈædvəkeɪt/ v./n. 提倡；倡导者 She is a strong advocate for women's rights. 她是女权的坚定倡导者。
aggressive /əˈɡresɪv/ adj. 侵略性的；积极进取的 The company has adopted an aggressive marketing strategy. 公司采用了积极进取的营销策略。
allocate /ˈæləkeɪt/ v. 分配 The funds were allocated to various departments. 资金被分配给了各个部门。
analogy /əˈnælədʒi/ n. 类比 He drew an analogy between the brain and a computer. 他将大脑与计算机进行了类比。
anonymous /əˈnɒnɪməs/ adj. 匿名的 The donation was made by an anonymous benefactor. 这笔捐款来自一位匿名捐助者。
appeal /əˈpiːl/ v./n. 呼吁；吸引力 The idea of working abroad appeals to many young people. 出国工作的想法吸引了很多年轻人。
assess /əˈses/ v. 评估 We need to assess the risks before making a decision. 我们需要在做决定之前评估风险。
assign /əˈsaɪn/ v. 分配；指派 The teacher assigned homework to the students. 老师给学生布置了作业。
assist /əˈsɪst/ v. 帮助 The nurse assisted the doctor during the operation. 护士在手术中协助医生。
assume /əˈsjuːm/ v. 假设；承担 We cannot assume that the trend will continue. 我们不能假设这种趋势会持续。
authorize /ˈɔːθəraɪz/ v. 授权 Only the manager can authorize such expenses. 只有经理才能授权此类开支。
aware /əˈweə(r)/ adj. 意识到的 People are becoming more aware of environmental issues. 人们越来越意识到环境问题。
capture /ˈkæptʃə(r)/ v. 捕获；拍摄 The photographer captured a beautiful moment. 摄影师捕捉到了一个美丽的瞬间。
cease /siːs/ v. 停止 The factory ceased production last month. 工厂上个月停止了生产。
chronic /ˈkrɒnɪk/ adj. 慢性的；长期的 Chronic stress can lead to health problems. 长期压力会导致健康问题。
clarify /ˈklærɪfaɪ/ v. 澄清 Could you clarify your position on this issue? 你能澄清你对这个问题的立场吗？
compel /kəmˈpel/ v. 强迫 The evidence compelled him to change his mind. 证据迫使他改变了想法。
compose /kəmˈpəʊz/ v. 组成；创作 Water is composed of hydrogen and oxygen. 水由氢和氧组成。
comprise /kəmˈpraɪz/ v. 包含；由…组成 The committee comprises ten members. 委员会由十名成员组成。
conform /kənˈfɔːm/ v. 遵从；符合 All products must conform to safety standards. 所有产品必须符合安全标准。
conscience /ˈkɒnʃəns/ n. 良心 He could not ignore his conscience. 他无法忽视自己的良心。
consent /kənˈsent/ n./v. 同意 Informed consent is required before the procedure. 手术前需要知情同意。
consolidate /kənˈsɒlɪdeɪt/ v. 巩固；合并 The company consolidated its market position. 公司巩固了其市场地位。
constrain /kənˈstreɪn/ v. 约束；限制 Budget constraints limit our options. 预算限制了我们的选择。
controversy /ˈkɒntrəvɜːsi/ n. 争论 The decision sparked a heated controversy. 这个决定引发了一场激烈的争论。
correspond /ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd/ v. 对应；通信 The results correspond with our predictions. 结果与我们的预测一致。
crisis /ˈkraɪsɪs/ n. 危机 The economic crisis affected millions of people. 经济危机影响了数百万人。
